---
version: 2.0.2
title: enums: invalid declarations and patterns
file: ./test/enum_parser_test.gleam
test_name: invalid_enums_snapshot_test
---
Source:
module main

enum Box(a) is Thing {
  Full(Int)
  Empty
  let x = 1
  describe() { "box" }
}

enum Nothing {}

enum Light { Red, Red }

class Loud is Light {}

main() {
  match Light.Red {
    Light.Red() -> 1
    _ -> 2
  }
}

---
error: enums cannot be generic
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:3:9
  │
3 │ enum Box(a) is Thing {
  │         ─┬─
  │          ╰─ type parameters are not allowed here
  ╰─

`Box` is an enum: its variants carry no data, so it has nothing to be generic over.

error: enums cannot inherit
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:3:13
  │
3 │ enum Box(a) is Thing {
  │             ────┬───
  │                 ╰─ enums have no superclass or interfaces
  ╰─

`Box` is an enum: a closed set of values. It cannot extend a class or implement an interface.

error: enum variants carry no data
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:4:3
  │
4 │   Full(Int)
  │   ────┬────
  │       ╰─ `Full` cannot hold values
  ╰─

An enum variant is a single named value. When alternatives need different data, use a closed class hierarchy instead.

help: Write `class Full(...) is Base` for each alternative that carries data.

error: enums contain only variants
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:6:3
  │
6 │   let x = 1
  │   ────┬────
  │       ╰─ expected a variant name
  ╰─

The body of `Box` may only list variant names, such as `Error`. Enums have no fields, constructors or methods.

help: Write functions that take the enum as a parameter, or use a class.

error: enums contain only variants
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:7:3
  │
7 │   describe() { "box" }
  │   ──────────┬─────────
  │             ╰─ expected a variant name
  ╰─

The body of `Box` may only list variant names, such as `Error`. Enums have no fields, constructors or methods.

help: Write functions that take the enum as a parameter, or use a class.

error: empty enum
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:10:6
   │
10 │ enum Nothing {}
   │      ───┬───
   │         ╰─ this enum has no variants
   ╰─

`Nothing` has no values, so no value of it could ever exist.

help: List at least one variant, such as `Error`.

error: enum patterns take no arguments
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:18:14
   │
18 │     Light.Red() -> 1
   │              ─┬
   │               ╰─ remove these parentheses
   ╰─

`Light.Red` is a value, not a constructor, so it is matched as written.

Found 7 errors.

